If this thread is for beginners, then there should be a warning label
on the whole displacement discussion.  Beginners should be running
straight for a chokepoint when they are being attacked by multiple
monsters.  Beginners should NOT be hanging out in giant open spaces so
that they can take full advantage of displacement.

I am also very much against encouraging beginners to throw daggers at
everything.  Beginners should be learning which monsters are a threat
to their character.  Throwing daggers at everything does not teach
people risk assessment, which is a really valuable thing to know.


